    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just that the \"cost\" feels so heavy lately. like, everything is just effort for the sake of effort, and there's no real payoff at the end of it. if you're playing a game where the rules are rigged and the house always wins, and the only way to stop playing is to walk away from the table entirely... isn't it just more logical to walk away than to keep draining your resources on a losing hand?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
